@host = http://localhost:4000/api/v1
@email = juan.test@test.com
@password = password123

### Health
GET {{host}}/health

### Registrar usuario  (si repites, da 409; cambia @email)
# @name register
POST {{host}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nombre": "Juan",
  "apellido": "Pérez",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Login  (guarda los tokens)
# @name login
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Me  (perfil del usuario autenticado)
GET {{host}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Me sin token  → 401 UNAUTHORIZED
GET {{host}}/auth/me

### Me con token inválido  → 401 UNAUTHORIZED
GET {{host}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer token-de-mentira

### Refresh  (rota el par de tokens)
# @name refresh
POST {{host}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{login.response.body.$.refreshToken}}"
}

### Refresh con token VIEJO  → 401 (reuso; además revoca la familia)
POST {{host}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{login.response.body.$.refreshToken}}"
}

### Refresh sin token  → 400 con errors[]
POST {{host}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Logout  (revoca el refresh token del login)
POST {{host}}/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{login.response.body.$.refreshToken}}"
}

### Refresh tras logout  → 401 (token revocado)
POST {{host}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{login.response.body.$.refreshToken}}"
}

### 404
GET {{host}}/no-existe
